Package: hd-kernel-desktop
Version: @META_DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: linux-image-@RELEASE@ (= @KERNEL_DEB_VERSION@),
 zfs-modules-@RELEASE@ (= @ZFS_DEB_VERSION@)
Conflicts: hd-kernel, hd-kernel-vm, hd-kernel-server, linux-image-amd64, linux-headers-amd64,
 linux-base-amd64, zfs-dkms
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian kernel for desktops and laptops
 Depends on the most recent HyprDebian kernel for desktops of @SUITE@ and its
 ZFS module, so that they are installed and upgraded with it. The kernel is
 that of hd-kernel, linux @KERNEL_VERSION@ of Debian with its patches and its
 config, but of the drivers only those of the hardware of desktops and laptops,
 of what people plug in and of software; the ZFS module is that of zfs-linux
 @ZFS_VERSION@, built against it. Both are built on the build server and
 signed with a key that is made for the build and thrown away, so a system
 needs neither DKMS nor a compiler for ZFS, and the kernel trusts no other key
 for its modules.
 .
 It replaces the kernel of Debian and the other HyprDebian kernels, and DKMS
 for ZFS: installing it removes hd-kernel, hd-kernel-vm, hd-kernel-server,
 linux-image-amd64, linux-headers-amd64, linux-base-amd64 and zfs-dkms, so DKMS
 builds no ZFS module that the kernel does not trust.
 See hd-kernel-desktop(7).
